  "notes": "M1/M2/M7 on profile t0 (Apple M2 Max, Docker Desktop, shared dev host, ~30 other containers running - absolute latency carries VM/overlay and host-noise overhead; the with/without delta is the load-bearing figure). Latency: independent open-loop generator (measure latency) hitting schild-api vs site-api directly on the sites network, 50/500/2000 rps, 20 s, 3 s warmup. Headline M1 kill criterion: p95 overhead at 500 rps = 0.81 ms (<5 ms). K3 (measure k3): resilience corpus under concurrent benign load; every malicious payload was rejected or answered 503 on timeout (fail-closed), never passed. M2/T19 (measure egress + egress-check): 60 attack requests through the stripper with canary values in path/query/body/cookie/user-agent and canary source IPs (v4+v6); the independent egress-check found 0 leaks over 1053 signals. The t0 smoke additionally cross-checked the client transparency log against each lab's received signals (IP-free). M7/B02: request-path p99 is unchanged (within noise) with all labs down and with all labs+relays down, 0 request errors; Grundschutz stayed active. T12 (fix-owner rerun at 2026-10-26T20:46:36Z on the rebuilt schild:mvp sha256:8603b52304b0..., whose only change against sha256:2981cbdb... is the embedded dashboard build): live in t0 with the new compose profile t12 (front-api = `schild front` -> schild-t12 on 127.0.0.1 in the front's network namespace, app site-api), driven by testlab/scripts/t12.sh (make testlab-t12): kill under load, dead, restarted, hung (docker pause), resumed. Fail-open only on connection refused (process dead); a hung schild gives 503 after the 3 s front timeout and nothing reaches the app. All other numbers in this file are from the earlier run on sha256:2981cbdb....",
